{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache` is a concrete, cloneable type.\nCloning it shares its state and takes constant time in the number of interned nodes and cached outlines.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct ValidationCache<D: Domain> { /* private fields */ }\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> Clone for ValidationCache<D>;\nimpl<D: Domain> Default for ValidationCache<D>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations**\n1. `ValidationCache` is a concrete, cloneable type.\n2. Cloning shares state.\n3. Cloning takes constant time in the number of interned nodes and cached outlines.\n4. The type implements `Clone` and `Default`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[cloning_a_configured_cache_shares_its_agent_sources_and_observations]` clones a configured cache. It then asserts `Arc::ptr_eq` on `agent`, `sources`, `source_addresses`, `outlines` and `usage`. Pointer sharing is what makes the clone constant-time. A deep copy of the interned nodes or cached outlines would fail these assertions.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[clones_interning_the_same_data_concurrently_get_one_handle]` covers the private `nodes` field. Four clones intern the same data concurrently and all get the same id. The original cache then resolves that id with `node_data`, and a different value gets a different id. This shows the node table is shared with the clones and is not copied.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` covers shared outlines. A cloned domain returns the same cached outline for a path (`std::ptr::eq`), even after the file changes or is removed. A fresh cache sees the new content, so the sharing comes from the clone.\n\nI read `impl[ValidationCache<D>/Clone]/fn[clone]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs`. It clones all six fields, and all of them are `Arc` or `Option<Arc>`. The tests are consistent with that.\n\n**Default and concrete type**\nThe requirement states no behavior for `Default` beyond the impl existing. The tests use `ValidationCache::<Application>::new()`. They also use `Default::default()` for caches inside domains, and `Application::default().cache()`, which needs the `Default` impl. Using the type this way also confirms it is concrete.\n\nI found no gap.",
